<title>BRAZIL: Brazil corn crop back at pre-drought levels - Safras.</title>
<headline>Brazil corn crop back at pre-drought levels - Safras.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's 1996/97 corn crop should reach 33.47 million tonnes, marking a complete recovery from last year's drought-hit crop of 30.46 million tonnes, said consultants Safras e Mercado.</p>
<p>The 1996/97 harvest compares with a 1994/95 crop of 33.05 million tonnes and shows that farmers have kept planted area the same and that the 10 percent increase is entirely due to expectations of normal weather, Safras said.</p>
<p>With domestic consumption estimated at 33.40 million tonnes, imports should be reduced to 390,000 tonnes next year, mainly in the northeast, against this year's 500,000 tonnes, it added.</p>
<p>-- Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
